-# Windows readonly verification broker and synthetic probes
+# Windows read-only verification backend
 
-SPS §9.2.4 / D23 defines the product boundary. `LpacVerificationMain` accepts only
-the Runtime-private frozen plan and hash, fixed Node/Daemon assets and limits.
-It provides execution, independent inspection and owned recovery; application
-output is separate from trusted control receipts. Current acceptance and any
-uncompleted deployment work belong in `docs/project-status.md`.
+SPS §9.2.4 / D23 and the subordinate Windows verification contract define this backend. The production entry is LpacVerificationMain, built by scripts/lib/verification-asset-producer.ts. Runtime never downloads/compiles a launcher or selects an arbitrary host program.
 
-The public broker uses DETACHED creation, actual child policy1, Job1 and Node
-no-addons. Job association is atomic at creation and verified before resume.
-The legacy synthetic entry points retain their original profiles and evidence;
-their existence does not register them as product execution backends.
+Only the approved windows-lpac-node-single-process-readonly/v1 profile is adopted: pinned Node 24.19.0 x64, LPAC with the approved single registryRead capability, child policy1, DETACHED creation, no-addons, Job1 and fixed filesystem/network/resource limits. Non-Windows, additional processes, addons, dependencies and unproved declarations are rejected.
 
-Compile all `.cs` files in this directory with the existing x64 .NET Framework
-compiler, `/reference:System.Web.Extensions.dll`, `/reference:System.Management.dll`
-and explicit `/main:LpacVerificationMain` for the product. The build-time producer
-is `scripts/lib/verification-asset-producer.ts`; Runtime never compiles code.
-For synthetic probes only, select `/main:LpacStartupPoc`. The private native helper uses explicit
-`/main:LpacPrivateRegistryChild` and its frozen source set. Preserve each build
-and its raw hashes before execution; do not substitute a newer executable for
-an archived attempt. Guest native reports use `LpacProbeJson`, avoiding the
-observed guest finalizer failures associated with the System.Web reporting path.
+Real sf-orchestrator owns sf_verification_plan; real sf-verifier owns sf_verification_run. Code permission stays separate. Plans and attempts bind actual owner/state/subject, immutable inputs and execution assets, budgets, normalized argv, invocation lease and trusted termination receipts. Application output cannot impersonate control evidence.
 
-The D22 primary native boundary helper uses `/main:LpacSingleNativeBoundary`;
-it performs the fixed native API calls directly in the single primary process.
-`--synthetic-single-files` is the fixed file/alias/network probe, and
-`--synthetic-single-resource-{wall,cancel,output,memory,crash,daemon-crash}` are
-finite resource/lifecycle probes. Resource rejection intentionally returns owner1;
-the lab driver proves expected rejection without turning it into application success.
+Cancellation/recovery uses the same attempt and verifies stable process/resource ownership, Job cleanup and preserved failure history. Missing numeric exit, stale/tampered/incomplete receipts or unknown cleanup cannot pass shared evidence consumers, Formal Version or Close.
 
-`--synthetic-registry-read-node-file-locked` and
-`--synthetic-registry-read-node-test-file-locked` accept only their fixed
-first-party probe. Both preserve symlink paths and select TAP explicitly; the
-second uses `--test --test-isolation=none positive.cjs` in the frozen input cwd.
-Real application/owner exits were0, the module stayed unchanged and its write
